      "title": "Upload concurrency of ingest import",
      "question": "How does import throughput grow with the number of models uploaded in parallel, and where does it stop paying off?",
      "answer": "It grows with diminishing returns: 1 to 8 uploaders take the import from 40 to 88 MB/s (2.2 times), each doubling helping less (1.49, 1.27, 1.17 times) as every upload slows down on storage shared with the rest of the stack; the default of 4 stays until the sweep is repeated against storage over a network.",
